# SkySpy vLLM — recommended config, DEPLOYED to sip-ai-vllm on the DGX Spark 2026-07-24.
#
# Model: the station's own Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8 (MoE, fast on the GB10). The tuning
# takeaways applied at REAL big context (NOT compact mode — 8192 was rejected: it
# only scored well by degrading the assistant's prompt):
#   - max_model_len 65536  : full context, well above the ~47k full-mode prompt peak
#   - kv_cache_dtype fp8    : the consistent tuning win — halves KV so 65536 fits at
#                             gpu-util 0.50, and boosts decode throughput
#   - max_num_seqs 16, max_num_batched_tokens 8192 : better batching than the old 8
#   - gpu_memory_utilization 0.50 : KEPT — sip-ai-vllm coexists with the sip-ai GPU
#                             stack (speaches, etc.); do not raise without pausing them
#
# For the skyspy compose `vllm` service, the equivalent .env:
VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-FP8
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=65536
VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.50
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=16
VLLM_MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192
VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
VLLM_TOOL_PARSER=hermes
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--enable-chunked-prefill
# GB10 note: needs VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=0 (DeepGemm FP8 MoE asserts on Blackwell);
# gpu-util ceiling ~0.85 (128 GB unified). On a dedicated full-GPU box, raise
# gpu-util and max_num_seqs for more throughput.
#
# NOTE on the earlier sweeps: the reward's short golden evals are noisy (±0.15) for
# this model and can't see long-context value, so they favored tiny contexts. Fixed
# by pinning max_model_len big and dropping it from the search. Models too big for
# 128 GB unified (Ling-2.6-flash-FP8 98 GB, Mistral bench-hang) were screened out.
